  "topic": "DEEP DIVE & SYNTAX",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; width: 100%;\"><div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 8px; width: 100%;\"><div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 12px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">Deep Dive</div><h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 32px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: -0.5px;\">Data Types & <hlt>Memory Models</hlt></h1><p style=\"font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 600px;\">How variables allocate space and manage values inside computer memory.</p></div><div style=\"background: #fef08a; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 22px; box-sizing: border-box;\"><span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">1. Fundamentals</span><h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 12px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">Primitive Python Types</h2><p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 14px 0; line-height: 1.5;\">In Python, every value has an explicit data type that tells the system how many bytes of memory are needed:</p><div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 12px;\"><div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 10px 14px;\"><strong style=\"color: #2563eb; font-family: 'Title', monospace;\">int</strong>: Whole numbers like <hlt>42</hlt>, <hlt>-7</hlt></div><div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 10px 14px;\"><strong style=\"color: #2563eb; font-family: 'Title', monospace;\">float</strong>: Decimal numbers like <hlt>3.14</hlt>, <hlt>0.005</hlt></div><div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 10px 14px;\"><strong style=\"color: #2563eb; font-family: 'Title', monospace;\">str</strong>: Text sequences like <hlt>\"Adhicode\"</hlt></div><div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 10px 14px;\"><strong style=\"color: #2563eb; font-family: 'Title', monospace;\">bool</strong>: Truth values <hlt>True</hlt> or <hlt>False</hlt></div></div></div><div style=\"background: #93c5fd; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 22px; box-sizing: border-box;\"><span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">2. Dynamic Typing</span><h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">Variables Point to Objects</h2><p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 12px 0; line-height: 1.5;\">Python variables act as <hlt>name tags attached to values</hlt>. You can reassign a variable to a completely different type at runtime without crashing.</p><div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\">score = <span style=\"color: #7ee787;\">100</span>          <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Initially an integer</span><br/>score = <span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"High Score\"</span>  <span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Now a string reference!</span></div></div></div>"
}
